>
>     If any of these answers are true, it means that it is a design specific issue of Affymetrix Exon Array.

Affymetrix put down a large set of PMs and MMs (and a few more probes)
when they designed the chip type.  Then they provided a CDF matching
this.  Afterwards others have created various types of custom CDFs,
each containing a subset of these PMs & MMs.  Thus, as the above
shows, it is a combination of the original Affymetrix chip type design
and choice of CDF.

>    To what extent they can influence on further analysis, such as differential expression analysis, or splice
>    variance analysis.

I don't think it will affect it at all or only very little, but I
leave it for others who have done more HuEx-1_0-st-v2 analyses to
pitch in here.

I leave the rest of your questions also for the exon experts who
designed those CDFs.

Hope this helps

